
# 🗂️ NCBI Data Retrieval Module

This directory serves as the central hub for local NCBI datasets retrieved for sequence parsing, comparative genomics, and downstream molecular docking preparation within the internship repository.

---

## 📁 Directory Architecture

```text
NCBI_Data_Retrieval/
├── Nucleotide_Sequences/   # Local nucleotide datasets (mRNA, viral & bacterial genomes)
└── Protein_Sequence/       # Local amino acid datasets (enzymes, receptors, biomarkers)

```

## 🔬 Subdirectory Overview

### 🧬 [Nucleotide_Sequences](https://www.google.com/search?q=./Nucleotide_Sequences/)

Contains local FASTA and GenBank sequence files spanning human, mouse, viral, and bacterial genomes:

* **`NM_000518.5`** — Human Hemoglobin Subunit Beta (*HBB*) mRNA
* **`NC_045512.2`** — SARS-CoV-2 Wuhan-Hu-1 Complete Genome
* **`NM_007294.4`** — Human BRCA1 DNA Repair Associated mRNA
* **`NC_000913.3`** — *E. coli* K-12 MG1655 Complete Chromosome
* **`M13241.1`** — Mouse GAPDH Gene Fragment

### 🧪 [Protein_Sequence](https://www.google.com/search?q=./Protein_Sequence/)

Contains local amino acid sequence files and structural targets for functional analysis and molecular docking workflows:

* **`NP_000509.1`** — Human Hemoglobin Subunit Beta Protein
* **`YP_009724390.1`** — SARS-CoV-2 Spike Glycoprotein
* **`NP_007295.1`** — Human BRCA1 Tumor Suppressor Protein
* **`NP_415492.1`** — *E. coli* K-12 DNA Polymerase I
* **`NP_032110.1`** — Mouse GAPDH Metabolic Control Protein

---

## 🛠️ Module Objectives

1. **Offline Sequence Processing:** Provide static benchmark data to parse headers, extract CDS region features, and calculate physicochemical properties without continuous API dependencies.
2. **Genomic to Proteomic Translation:** Facilitate cross-referencing between DNA/mRNA sequences and their corresponding translated protein products.
3. **Pipeline Input Preparation:** Supply validated datasets for gene expression scripts, sequence alignment, and target protein prep for docking studies.

